    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Canada Council for the Arts The arts and their contributions are crucial to society—they stimulate the economy and foster social cohesion and Canadian unity. The Canada Council for the Arts encourages public participation in the arts from coast to coast to coast, thereby contributing to the recognition of artists and arts organizations from Canada abroad. That’s why the Council is proud to support the 26th edition of the MUTEK Festival, which is not only a reflection of its community, but also a fantastic showcase for arts in Canada and around the world. Michelle Chawla , Director and CEO of the Canada Council for the Arts Canada Economic Development Canada Economic Development for Quebec Regions is proud to support MUTEK, a festive gathering with creativity at its heart, showcasing the metropolis and enabling it to move to the beat of electronic music and digital art. Tourisme Montréal Tourisme Montréal is proud to support MUTEK, a festival that offers visitors a completely different way to experience the city. Through electronic music, digital arts, and immersive installations, MUTEK showcases an innovative, creative, and boldly contemporary Montréal."
      }
    ],
