        "@id": "https://montreal.mutek.org/en/artists/eva-papamargariti"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Eva Papamargariti  GR/UK — As They Were Drifting Away, Their Bodies Turned Into Waves  Eva Papamargariti ’s video work As they were drifting away, their bodies turned into waves focuses on the dialectics of fluidity and motion, and entanglement between bodies — critters and the traces left as they float, sink, disperse, and get cast in and out of water. Her piece attempts to manifest the ways selfhood and desires emerge in the midst of constant political, geological and technological flows. How can this drifting create a new paradigm allowing for coexistence through symbiotic forms of action?  With the support of the Stavros Niarchos Foundation (SNF)"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Eva Papamargariti"
      }
    ]
  },
