      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Gilles Tarabiscuité  CA/QC — Visions du monde numérique  How does one create digital art without a computer? How does one take pictures that resemble computer-generated images, yet remain “true” photographs, without any alterations or digital editing? This is the goal of Visions du monde numérique . With simple cardboard polygons and wooden shapes on which he glues pictures of various objects and subjects, Gilles Tarabiscuité manages to create works unrivaled by the best Photoshop experts, in a truly analog way."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Gilles Tarabiscuité"
      }
    ]
  },
